{"tool_name":"rmats","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"rmats","identifiers":["doi:10.1073/pnas.1419161111","doi:10.1007/978-1-62703-514-9_10","doi:10.1093/nar/gkr1291"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Mats is a computational tool to detect differential alternative splicing events from rna-seq data.","home_url":"http://rnaseq-mats.sourceforge.net","keywords":["Alternative Splicing","Bayes Theorem","Brain","Cell Line, Tumor","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Multivariate Analysis","RNA-Binding Proteins","Reverse Transcriptase Polymerase Chain Reaction","Sequence Analysis, RNA","RNA-Seq","Gene Expression"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"rmats","home":"http://rnaseq-mats.sourceforge.net/","license":"BSD-2-Clause","summary":"MATS is a computational tool to detect differential alternative splicing events from RNA-Seq data.","addition_date":"2022-03-21T20:02:01.592637Z","last_update_date":"2022-03-21T20:03:03.109552Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Workbench"],"version":["4.1.2"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:rmats","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Juw Won Park"},{"name":"Lan Lin"},{"name":"Michael D Henry"},{"name":"Qing Zhou"},{"name":"Shihao Shen"},{"name":"Yi Xing"},{"name":"Ying Nian Wu"},{"name":"Zhi-xiang Lu"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/Xinglab/rmats-turbo"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"},{"term":"SAM","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2573"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Splicing analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2499"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"P-value","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1669"}},{"data":{"term":"Q-value","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3932"}}]}],"name":"rMATS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1419161111","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2014, National Academy of Sciences. All rights reserved.Ultra-deep RNA sequencing (RNA-Seq) has become a powerful approach for genome-wide analysis of pre-mRNA alternative splicing. We previously developed multivariate analysis of transcript splicing (MATS), a statisticalmethod for detecting differential alternative splicing between two RNA-Seq samples. Here we describe a new statistical model and computer program, replicate MATS (rMATS), designed for detection of differential alternative splicing from replicate RNASeq data. rMATS uses a hierarchical model to simultaneously account for sampling uncertainty in individual replicates and variability among replicates. In addition to the analysis of unpaired replicates, rMATS also includes a model specifically designed for paired replicates between sample groups. The hypothesis-testing framework of rMATS is flexible and can assess the statistical significance over any user-defined magnitude of splicing change. The performance of rMATS is evaluated by the analysis of simulated and real RNA-Seq data. rMATS outperformed two existing methods for replicate RNA-Seq data in all simulation settings, and RTPCR yielded a high validation rate (94%) in an RNA-Seq dataset of prostate cancer cell lines. Our data also provide guiding principles for designing RNA-Seq studies of alternative splicing. We demonstrate that it is essential to incorporate biological replicates in the study design. Of note, pooling RNAs or merging RNA-Seq data from multiple replicates is not an effective approach to account for variability, and the result is particularly sensitive to outliers. The rMATS source code is freely available at rnaseq-mats.sourceforge. net/. As the popularity of RNA-Seq continues to grow, we expect rMATS will be useful for studies of alternative splicing in diverse RNA-Seq projects.","authors":[{"name":"Henry M.D."},{"name":"Lin L."},{"name":"Lu Z.-X."},{"name":"Park J.W."},{"name":"Shen S."},{"name":"Wu Y.N."},{"name":"Xing Y."},{"name":"Zhou Q."}],"citationCount":739,"date":"2014-12-23T00:00:00Z","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","title":"rMATS: Robust and flexible detection of differential alternative splicing from replicate RNA-Seq data"},"pmcid":"PMC4280593","pmid":"25480548","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"RNA splicing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3320"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"rMATS","home":"https://bio.tools/rmats","license":"BSD-2-Clause","version":"4.1.2","summary":"MATS is a computational tool to detect differential alternative splicing events from RNA-Seq data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rmats:4.1.2/cmd/rnaseq-mats.sourceforge.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":1657,"citations":[{"count":3,"year":"-1"},{"count":7,"year":"2015"},{"count":34,"year":"2016"},{"count":48,"year":"2017"},{"count":75,"year":"2018"},{"count":82,"year":"2019"},{"count":134,"year":"2020"},{"count":154,"year":"2026"},{"count":168,"year":"2021"},{"count":223,"year":"2022"},{"count":233,"year":"2023"},{"count":238,"year":"2024"},{"count":258,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1419161111","pmcid":"PMC4280593","pmid":"25480548","ref_count":37,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":2,"year":"2008"},{"count":3,"year":"2014"},{"count